translate en b26_001:
    "The door chime sounds heavier than usual. Or maybe it's just Kai's ears. Gema Masa is quiet this afternoon — Pak Ageng's rocking chair sits empty, still creaking softly before coming to a stop on its own."

translate en b26_002:
    kai_hati "Pak Ageng isn't at the counter. Weird. {i}(glancing toward the darkest corner of the shop){/i} …And my eyes go straight there again. That glass cabinet."

translate en b26_003:
    "Kai steps closer. Behind the lightly fogged glass, red Type IV Metal cassettes sit lined up in neat rows. Right in the middle row, a single handwritten white label stares back at him: {b}6 MONTHS AHEAD (AUGUST 1){/b}."

translate en b26_004:
    kai_hati "August first. Graduation results day. The day Yara leaves for her dream university out of town. The date that decides… whether I still have a melody, or go right back to being an empty shell."

translate en b26_005:
    "Kai presses his palm against the cold glass. His breath fogs it up."

translate en b26_006:
    kai "{i}(whispering){/i} Just one minute. I just need to hear one minute of August first. If it's her laughing… I'll go home. I'll get through these six months calmly. No more panicking. I promise."

translate en b26_007:
    kai_hati "My hand's already on the cabinet key. Pak Ageng never pulls that little key out of the lock. Just one turn…"

translate en b26_008:
    ageng "You know, Kai."

translate en b26_009:
    "Kai flinches. He yanks his hand off the key like he just touched a hot coal. At the back door of the shop, Pak Ageng stands holding a small tray — two cups of coffee, still steaming."

translate en b26_010:
    ageng "{i}(walking over to the counter, setting the cups down){/i} The hardest cassette tape to fix is the one we tangle up ourselves. All because we're too scared to hear how the song ends."

translate en b26_011:
    kai "Pak, I— I was just…"

translate en b26_012:
    ageng "I know what you're looking for behind that glass. {i}(looking at Kai for a long moment, not angry — just sad){/i} That red August first tape is expensive, Kai. More expensive than any tape you've ever bought."

translate en b26_013:
    kai "The price… it's not money, is it, Pak?"

translate en b26_014:
    ageng "No. To peek six months ahead, you can't just pay with the taste of some dish, or where you left your motorbike keys. {i}(standing right in front of Kai){/i} The price is your single happiest memory. Pulled straight out of your head, spooled onto this tape, gone for good. You won't be able to remember it again. No matter how hard you try."

translate en b26_015:
    kai "{i}(swallowing hard){/i} My single happiest memory…"

translate en b26_016:
    kai_hati "And my head immediately replays all of them. Hot rawon by the train tracks in the rain. The wind at the top of Bukit Banyak. Boiling water in the canteen. And right at the very top… the city library."

translate en b26_016_p2:
    kai_hati "Books tumbling down. Dust floating in the sunset light. And Yara standing there — the exact second I realized I wasn't going to die. That's my anchor. That's what turned me from a scared ghost into… a real person."

translate en b26_017a:
    kai "{i}(his voice barely a whisper){/i} …I'll do it, Pak."

translate en b26_018a:
    kai_hati "The fear of losing her already won. I'm willing to throw away my past, as long as my future is safe. It makes sense. It… it makes sense."

translate en b26_019a:
    ageng "{i}(letting out a heavy sigh){/i} That's a very brave choice, kid. And a very foolish one."

translate en b26_020a:
    "Pak Ageng opens the glass cabinet, takes out the red cassette labeled AUGUST 1, and sets it down on the counter."

translate en b26_021a:
    ageng "Before the tape does its work, you get to choose. Which memory are you giving up? This tape doesn't take at random — it takes the one you point it to."

translate en b26_022a:
    ageng "Put your hand on top of the cassette. Think of that moment. Let the tape draw the sounds, the images, and the feeling right out of you."

translate en b26_k1a:
    kai_hati "The city library. The smell of old paper. The sound of dust settling. The flush on her cheeks. And my heart pounding with impossible relief — I'm still alive. {i}(closing his eyes){/i} Take it. Just take it."

translate en b26_k1b:
    kai_hati "The rawon stall by the train tracks. Dark broth still steaming, rain pouring outside the tarp, her laughing because the chili got too hot. Warm. That's the warmest afternoon I've ever had. {i}(closing his eyes){/i} Take it. Just take it."

translate en b26_k1c:
    kai_hati "Bukit Banyak. That first gust of wind hitting our faces when we reached the top. She let out a little yelp, grabbing the tripod so it wouldn't tip over, then started laughing. The world felt huge and I wasn't scared. {i}(closing his eyes){/i} Take it. Just take it."

translate en b26_024a:
    "A sharp cold stings Kai's palm, shoots up his arm, and pierces straight into the center of his head. Suddenly his mind feels hollow — like a page got ripped cleanly out of the book of his life. A brief wave of dizziness. Then it's gone."

translate en b26_025a:
    kai "{i}(opening his eyes, frowning){/i} …Is it done, Pak?"

translate en b26_026a:
    ageng "{i}(sliding the red cassette into the player behind the counter){/i} It's done. The trade is settled."

translate en b26_027a:
    kai_hati "Weird. There's an empty space in my head. I know I know Yara. I know we're close, really close. But… how did it start? Where did we first talk? Why do we even wander around town together? {i}(pause){/i} Blank. A white page. —It's fine. It's fine. All that matters now is playing the tape."

translate en b26_017b:
    kai "Pak… I… {i}(his hands shaking, stepping back from the cabinet){/i} Give me some time. I can't decide right now. Temenan, Pak. I'm scared of picking wrong."

translate en b26_018b:
    ageng "{i}(watching Kai for a long moment, then nodding slowly){/i} Nggih. Time is a price too, Kai. Just a different way of paying."

translate en b26_019b:
    "Pak Ageng opens the glass cabinet, takes out the red cassette labeled AUGUST 1, and — right in front of Kai — puts it under the counter, in the easiest drawer to reach."

translate en b26_020b:
    ageng "I'll keep this tape right here. Until Friday. If you come back by Friday and say trade, we trade. If not… that's that. Means this tape wasn't meant for you."

translate en b26_021b:
    kai "What if someone else wants to buy it first, Pak?"

translate en b26_022b:
    ageng "{i}(smiling faintly, a little sad){/i} In this shop, the first person to make an offer isn't always the one who needs it most. Still, hesitate too long… and you usually lose your turn. Go on home, kid. Think it over carefully."

translate en b26_023b:
    kai_hati "Until Friday. Four days. Four days to figure out if I'm actually brave… or if I'm just putting off being a coward in a more polite way."

translate en b26_017c:
    kai "{i}(pulling his hand back from the cabinet, shaking his head){/i} No, Pak. {i}(his voice quiet, though no longer shaking){/i} Better I don't know. If the price for peace of mind is my happiest memory… that's not peace, Pak. That's a bad deal."

translate en b26_018c:
    ageng "{i}(nodding slowly, as if he'd expected as much){/i} Have a seat first. Drink your coffee. Your hands are still freezing."

translate en b26_019c:
    "Pak Ageng opens the glass cabinet, takes out the red cassette labeled AUGUST 1, wraps it in a clean cloth, and tucks it into a wooden drawer behind the counter — the same drawer where he keeps his late wife's tapes. Kai sees it. Pak Ageng knows Kai sees it."

translate en b26_020c:
    ageng "This tape won't be offered again. Not to you, not to anyone. Some things are better kept tucked away than sold."

translate en b26_021c:
    kai "Pak… thank you. {i}(pause){/i} I'm still scared, Pak. About August first. Still scared to death."

translate en b26_022c:
    ageng "Being scared is fine, kid. The dangerous part is letting your fear grab the wheel. {i}(pouring coffee){/i} Wes. Drink up. Let's talk about something else. What sounds did you say Yara's collecting these days?"

translate en bt_001:
    "Four days. Kai counts them down like he's waiting for something to blow up."

translate en bt_002:
    kai_hati "Monday: I'm sure I want to trade. Tuesday: I'm sure I don't. Wednesday: I'm sure I want to again — at two in the morning, staring at the ceiling. Thursday… Thursday I realize one thing. I'm not even thinking about the tape anymore. I'm trying to figure out how to decide without regretting it. And there's no answer to that."

translate en bt_003:
    "He still plays the regular tapes every night. Sixty seconds of tomorrow, sixty seconds of tomorrow. Safe. Under control. Yet every time the tape hiss stops, the exact same words pop back into his head: {i}until Friday.{/i}"

translate en bt_004:
    "Wednesday afternoon, his feet even carry him all the way to the mouth of the alley. He can see the shop from there — its wooden sign, its warm yellow window. Kai stands there for ten full minutes, like he's waiting for something to shove him from behind."

translate en bt_005:
    kai_hati "Go in right now, make the trade, get it over with. No need to wait for Friday. {i}(a long pause; his feet don't budge){/i} …Or go in right now, say never mind, get it over with that way. {i}(shaking his head, turning back home){/i} Turns out it's not making the choice I can't do. It's stopping myself from standing stuck in the middle."

translate en bt_006:
    "Thursday night, he writes two lines on scraps of paper, folds them, and throws them away. The first says: {i}\"I'll trade, Pak.\"{/i} The second says: {i}\"Never mind, Pak.\"{/i} Both go into the trash. Both feel like a lie."

translate en bt_007:
    kai_hati "I came later in the afternoon than usual. Half hoping the shop's already closed. The other half… I don't even know. My legs just walked themselves into this alley."

translate en bt_008a:
    "At the mouth of the alley, a man in a sharp suit has just walked out from the direction of the shop, carrying a small paper bag. He stops in his tracks when he sees Kai."

translate en bt_009a:
    kaya "{i}(smiling faintly){/i} Oh. We meet again."

translate en bt_010a:
    kai "{i}(freezing){/i} …Sir… were you just at the shop?"

translate en bt_011a:
    kaya "A small errand. {i}(lifting the paper bag slightly){/i} Good merchandise doesn't wait around for people who hesitate, kid. Remember that. {i}(walking past, his shoes splashing through a puddle){/i}"

translate en bt_012a:
    kai_hati "A paper bag. Cassette-sized. My chest goes ice cold."

translate en bt_008b:
    "The alley is deserted. Nobody's around except the orange cat under the potted plant, staring at Kai like usual. Still, the shop door is open, and from inside comes the creak of the rocking chair — slow, like an important guest just left."

translate en bt_013:
    kai "Pak… I'm here. About that red tape, I—"

translate en bt_014:
    ageng "{i}(raising one hand gently){/i} Sit down first, Kai."

translate en bt_015:
    "Pak Ageng steps behind the counter. He pulls open the drawer underneath — the drawer where he put the red AUGUST 1 cassette four days ago. It's empty. He leaves it open so Kai can see for himself."

translate en bt_016:
    kai "…It's empty."

translate en bt_017:
    ageng "Someone already took it."

translate en bt_018a:
    kai "That man, right, Pak? The one in the alley just now. The one who tried to buy this shop."

translate en bt_019a:
    ageng "He came Thursday afternoon. Paid without even asking the price. {i}(looking at Kai){/i} He knew the exact memory he wanted to trade. Didn't hesitate for a second. Sometimes I think… people who don't hesitate aren't braver. They just have less worth holding on to."

translate en bt_018b:
    kai "Who, Pak? Someone you know?"

translate en bt_019b:
    ageng "An old customer. Well-off man. Didn't say much — people who trade away memories rarely do. {i}(looking at Kai){/i} He came in, made his decision, and left. Thirty minutes, all done."

translate en bt_020:
    kai "{i}(sinking slowly into a chair, like his legs just gave out){/i} So… that's it? My chance… it's gone?"

translate en bt_021:
    ageng "Your chance at {i}that tape{/i} — yes, it's gone. {i}(pouring tea, sliding a cup over){/i} Listen, kid. You couldn't decide for four whole days. That wasn't a lack of an answer. That was an answer you weren't ready to hear."

translate en bt_022:
    kai "What do you mean, Pak?"

translate en bt_023:
    ageng "If you were temenan kepingin to know what's on August first, you would've traded back on Monday. What kept pulling you back and forth wasn't fear of the tape. You were scared of losing the memory you'd have to pay with. Which means that memory is still worth more to you than certainty. {i}(smiling slightly){/i} That's not bad news, Kai."

translate en bt_024:
    kai_hati "Weirdly enough… I'm relieved. Relieved and embarrassed and disappointed, all tangled together so I can't tell them apart. The tape's gone — not because I was brave enough to refuse, and not because I was brave enough to take it. Gone because I stood in the doorway too long."

translate en bt_025:
    kai "Pak… {i}(hesitating){/i} What did he hear, Pak? On August first. What… what sound did he hear?"

translate en bt_026:
    ageng "{i}(shaking his head gently){/i} Not your tape, not your story. What he heard was {i}his{/i} future — from his life, from his choices. Nothing to do with you. {i}(looking Kai straight in the eye){/i} And that's the last lesson from this tape, kid: your August first was never sold to anyone. It's still whole. Still unwritten. It can still… turn out any way at all."

translate en bt_027:
    kai "{i}(sitting quiet for a long moment){/i} …Any way at all. {i}(letting out a short, disbelieving laugh){/i} I spent four days terrified out of my mind — over something nobody else could even buy."

translate en bt_028:
    kai "So what now, Pak? August first is still coming. And I still don't know a thing."

translate en bt_029:
    ageng "You live through it. Like everyone else. Like Yara — she doesn't know what tomorrow looks like either, yet she still heads out collecting sounds every afternoon. {i}(standing up, straightening a shelf){/i} Wes, drink your tea. Go on home after this. And if you come by tomorrow, don't bring a face like you just missed the last train. The train may have left — but the station's still open."

translate en bt_030:
    kai_hati "The station's still open. {i}(pause){/i} I didn't get my certainty. Still, somehow, walking back down that alley, my steps don't feel as heavy as usual. Maybe because for the first time… tomorrow actually belongs to tomorrow again. Not to a cassette."

translate en b27r_001:
    "Pak Ageng presses play. The mechanical click sounds ridiculously loud in the quiet shop. Kai puts on the headphones. His heart pounds like it's trying to jump out of his chest."

translate en b27r_002:
    kai_hati "Sixty seconds. Her laugh. Please, let it be her laugh. Or street noise in Malang, or literally anything — just not—"

translate en b27r_003:
    kai_hati "Empty…? Why's it ten seconds of noth—"

translate en b27r_004:
    "It's not a laugh. Not a train, not boiling water. It's someone crying — so close Kai can hear the fabric of a jacket rustling. A jacket he knows."

translate en b27r_005:
    kai_hati "That's… that's Yara. That's Yara crying."

translate en b27r_006:
    "Silence settles back over the shop. Kai slowly pulls off the headphones. His hands are shaking so badly he almost drops them onto the counter. His face has gone pale. It feels like the tape player just drained every ounce of strength out of him."

translate en b27r_007:
    kai "{i}(choking up){/i} Why… {i}(staring at Pak Ageng, eyes hollow){/i} Why is she crying, Pak? Why does she have to say goodbye?"

translate en b27r_008:
    ageng "{i}(doesn't answer right away; ejects the red cassette and holds it out to Kai){/i} The tape never lies, Kai. Remember, though — the sound you just heard is the result of the road you picked today. You take this tape with you now. Along with that new hole in your memory."

translate en b27r_009:
    kai_hati "I paid with my happiest memory… for this. To hear her crying. To hear \"goodbye.\" The certainty I kept chasing turned out to be this."

translate en b27r_010a:
    "The water is freezing. Kai splashes his face three times, four times, until his breathing stops hitching. In the small cracked mirror in the corner, his face looks like a stranger's — at least it's stopped shaking."

translate en b27r_011a:
    ageng "{i}(from over by the counter, softly){/i} Water's the most honest thing there is, kid. Doesn't promise anything. Just feels cold, then runs right past."

translate en b27r_010b:
    "Kai slides down onto the wooden floor between the cassette shelves, pulling his knees to his chest. Pak Ageng doesn't tell him to get up. He just goes back to his rocking chair and lets the creak of the wood keep him company — slow, steady, like it's saying: this shop isn't in any hurry."

translate en b27r_010c:
    "Hands still shaking, Kai slips a regular cassette into his Walkman and presses play. Sixty seconds of tomorrow — canteen chatter, school bells, ordinary noise. Weirdly, those boring everyday sounds are what calm him down. Tomorrow is still there. The close, small tomorrow is still there."

translate en b27s_001:
    "Nothing special happens that afternoon. And that's the exact part Kai will remember for a long time: big days usually show up wearing an ordinary day's face."

translate en b27s_002:
    yara "{i}(hurrying up, canvas tote and recorder in hand, slightly out of breath){/i} Kai. You're here. Good. I've got something to tell you — hey, don't make that face yet, it's good news. Should be, anyway."

translate en b27s_003:
    kai "What news? Where'd you just run from, you're—"

translate en b27s_004:
    yara "School. They just posted the portfolio selection results. {i}(sitting on the porch step, looking at Kai with a wide smile but watchful eyes){/i} My portfolio got through, Kai. That university in Yogya… they accepted me. Sound design program. If nothing goes wrong, I'm leaving right after graduation. Early August."

translate en b27s_005:
    kai_hati "Yogya. Early August. August first. The date still came — only this time it came from Yara's own mouth, not off a cassette tape. And weirdly… it feels different. Not cold. Not like a death sentence. More like… news. Big news I was supposed to hear straight from her."

translate en b27s_006:
    kai "{i}(taking a breath, then smiling — forced for the first second, real by the second){/i} …Congrats, Yar. Seriously. That's what you've been chasing all along, right? All these sounds— {i}(pointing at her recorder){/i} —were for this."

translate en b27s_007:
    yara "{i}(studying Kai closely){/i} You're not surprised?"

translate en b27s_008:
    kai "I am. {i}(pause){/i} But you told me yourself. That… thanks. I mean — thanks for telling me face to face."

translate en b27s_009:
    yara "Well obviously I'd tell you face to face. What'd you think, I was gonna announce it on a cassette? {i}(laughing softly, then her voice drops gentler){/i} I'm scared too, Kai. New city, living alone in a boarding house, not knowing a single soul. Still, I've been kepingin this so badly. For a long time now."

translate en b27s_010:
    kai "I know. You can tell, from the way you collect sounds like you're packing snacks for a trip."

translate en b27s_011:
    yara "Speaking of packing for a trip. {i}(holding up her recorder){/i} I want to make one last recording before I leave. Like… a sound map of Malang. Every spot we've been to. So when I'm in Yogya and get homesick, I can just hit play."

translate en b27s_012:
    kai "We?"

translate en b27s_013:
    yara "Yeah, we. You think I can haul that tripod up Bukit Banyak by myself again? {i}(standing up, dusting off her pants){/i} Starting tomorrow. Afternoons, just like usual. Stay with me till my last day. Promise?"

translate en b27s_014:
    kai "{i}(pauses briefly — a tightness rises in his chest, but this time he doesn't run from it){/i} …Promise."

translate en b27s_015:
    kai_hati "Six months. Less than that, even. She's leaving, that's a fact, and it hurts — only it's the normal kind of hurt. Not crying trapped inside a tape. Not a riddle. Just… time moving forward. And I still have that time left to fill, not waste worrying."

translate en b27s_016:
    "Pak Ageng steps out of the shop carrying two cups of tea, like he's been listening the whole time — which he probably has."

translate en b27s_017:
    ageng "Heard someone passed selection. {i}(handing a cup to Yara){/i} Congratulations, kid. Yogya's a ways off… good sounds over there, though. Trains, morning markets, rain on boarding-house roofs. You're going to love collecting them."

translate en b27s_018:
    yara "{i}(taking the cup, beaming){/i} Thanks, Pak. I'll send recordings back from there, promise. That way your shop gets an out-of-town collection."

translate en b27s_019:
    ageng "{i}(glancing quietly at Kai){/i} Listen closely when the time comes, Kai. Some sounds only pass by once."

translate en b27s_020:
    kai_hati "I know what he means. And for once, I'm not running from it."

translate en b27s_021:
    yara "{i}(already a few steps down the path, looking back){/i} Hey, quit zoning out. Walk home with me. Let's stop by the rawon stall too, my treat. To celebrate."

translate en b27s_022:
    kai "{i}(getting up, catching up to her){/i} Treating me with scholarship money that hasn't even come in yet?"

translate en b27s_023:
    yara "With my allowance. So don't order anything expensive."

translate en b28_001a:
    "Kai wakes with a jolt, like he just fell from somewhere high up. His room looks exactly the same: papers on the desk, the digital clock, and the red plastic case sitting beside it."

translate en b28_002a:
    kai_hati "Something's wrong. I know something's wrong before I even know what."

translate en b28_003a:
    "He sits on the edge of the bed, rubbing his lightly throbbing head. Then he starts checking his memories one by one, like someone patting his pockets after getting pickpocketed."

translate en b28_004a:
    kai_hati "Yara. I know who she is. Girl from the class next door, collects noisy sounds from around town. We walk around the city together. Carry a tripod. Ate rawon by the train tracks in the rain. All the facts are right there. Neat. Logical. {i}(pause){/i} But the beginning… how did we even start?"

translate en b28_005a:
    "He tries to remember the city library. He knows he went there. He knows something happened — a stack of encyclopedias crashed right in front of his feet. Yet why did those books fall? Who knocked them over? What did Yara's face look like when their eyes first met through the afternoon dust?"

translate en b28_006a:
    kai_hati "Nothing. No picture. No sound of books hitting the floor. None of that heartbeat — the jolt when I realized I wasn't going to die. {i}(staring at his own hands){/i} My brain knows she matters. My chest… feels nothing. Like reading somebody else's biography who just happens to share my name."

translate en b28_007a:
    "Kai gets up and walks to his desk. His fingers brush the red cassette case — wound up inside that tape sits the most precious piece of himself, traded away for a peace of mind that turned out to be crying."

translate en b28_008a:
    kai_hati "I traded the heartbeat that made me feel alive… for a recording of her saying goodbye. {i}(slumping into his chair, staring out the window){/i} Way too expensive. Way too expensive, Kai."

translate en b28_001b:
    "Kai wakes with a jolt. The red plastic case sits next to the digital clock. And there's a strange blank spot in his head — not at the start of the story, right in the middle of it."

translate en b28_002b:
    kai_hati "I know we ate rawon by the train tracks. The facts are there: a tarp stall, pouring rain, a passing train making our spoons rattle. Yara brings it up all the time."

translate en b28_002b_p2:
    kai_hati "{i}(pause){/i} Yet the taste of the broth… the warmth… her laughing over spicy chili… {i}(shaking his head slowly){/i} Gone. Like somebody cut a whole scene out of a movie and spliced the ends back together. Clean seam. Missing scene."

translate en b28_003b:
    kai "{i}(slumping down, staring at the cassette case){/i} So that's what I paid. The warmest afternoon I had… just to hear her cry. {i}(a long pause){/i} No wonder Pak Ageng said it was expensive."

translate en b28_001c:
    "Kai wakes with a jolt. The red plastic case sits next to the digital clock. Outside the window, the morning breeze shifts the curtain — and that's where the hollowness hits."

translate en b28_002c:
    kai_hati "Bukit Banyak. I know we went up there. The photo's right on my phone — I can see it myself: me, her, the tripod, the city spread out below. {i}(staring at the photo for a long time){/i} Yet the wind… her little yelp when she almost slipped holding the tripod… that rush of relief realizing the world was huge and I wasn't scared… {i}(pause){/i} Nothing. All that's left is the picture. Proof with no feeling."

translate en b28_003c:
    kai "{i}(staring at the cassette case on his desk){/i} I traded the day I was brave… for a recording of the day she leaves. {i}(a short, bitter laugh){/i} Great deal, Kai. Real great deal."

translate en b28_009a:
    kai_hati "Last night at the shop, I splashed my face till the water didn't even feel cold anymore. This morning my head is clear — and because it's so clear, the shape of this hole stands out even sharper."

translate en b28_009b:
    kai_hati "Last night I sat on the shop floor for ages without saying a word. Pak Ageng didn't either. This morning my back aches — and that's the only thing I can actually feel. The rest is… a hole."

translate en b28_009c:
    kai_hati "Last night I listened to an ordinary tomorrow, and it calmed me down. This morning I woke up and realized: ordinary tomorrows just keep rolling on. The only thing missing is the yesterday that mattered most."

translate en b29r_001:
    "The sound of crying on the red tape loops in Kai's head like a scratched record. Every sob, every pause, and those two words: {i}goodbye.{/i} And Kai's cold brain lands on the harshest conclusion it can find."

translate en b29r_002:
    kai_hati "I'm the reason. It has to be me. If I stay close to her, I'm just walking her straight toward those tears. I'm the broken variable. If I step aside… she can leave smiling. Not crying. {i}(pause){/i} Sounds like protecting her. I know. I know it only sounds like it."

translate en b29r_003:
    "So the routine begins. Getting to school earlier so they don't cross paths at the gate. Skipping the hallway outside her class during break. And today: pretending to sleep, head buried on his desk in the empty classroom. Then — footsteps he knows. And the faint smell of lingering drizzle and mild soap."

translate en b29r_004:
    yara "Kai. {i}(softly){/i} Why aren't you answering my texts? We're recording the lathe at that workshop near the station this afternoon, right? I already borrowed spare batteries."

translate en b29r_005:
    "Kai's chest tightens like something's crushing it. He wants to look up. He wants to grab that canvas tote and go record like always. Then the crying on the tape slaps him awake."

translate en b29r_006:
    kai "{i}(slowly raising his head; his face flat, eyes blank){/i} Sorry, Yara. I'm busy. I need to start focusing on studying for finals. I can't help carry your gear around anymore."

translate en b29r_007:
    yara "{i}(taken aback){/i} Focusing on studying? {i}(repeating it with a bitter edge){/i} Yesterday we were still laughing on top of a hill, Kai. What's actually going on with you?"

translate en b29r_008:
    kai "{i}(looking away toward the whiteboard){/i} Nothing's going on. I just realized we don't have much time left. And I think… you should focus on your own portfolio too. Without me getting in the way."

translate en b29r_009:
    "Yara freezes for a few seconds. The silence between them this time isn't the hushed kind born of wonder — it's cold and sharp, and something cracks quietly right through the middle of it. Without another word, Yara turns and leaves. Her footsteps sound heavy."

translate en b29r_010:
    "Over the next few days, he follows his routine with cruel precision. Turning around in hallways. Hiding in a bathroom stall until the bell rings."

translate en b29r_010_p2:
    "Staring down at nothing on his phone when they pass on the stairs — while Yara's gaze follows him, full of questions, full of a wound starting to open. Until this afternoon, when Yara blocks his path at the empty back gate."

translate en b29r_011:
    yara "Why are you acting like this, Kai? {i}(standing right in front of him, bag slung loosely off one shoulder){/i} If I did something wrong, tell me. Don't just go silent like a coward and act like you don't know me. After everything we've been through!"

translate en b29r_012:
    kai_hati "Tell her. Just tell her about the stupid red tape. Tell her, and end it. {i}(pause — then the hole in his head yawns open){/i} …Except I don't even remember how we started. Even my first heartbeat around her is gone. All that's left is fear of her crying on August first. And my mouth picks the safest line for that fear."

translate en b29r_013:
    kai "{i}(looking straight at Yara, forcing his eyes to stay cold){/i} Nothing's wrong, Yara. I just realized… we never really fit together anyway. You live in your world full of noise."

translate en b29r_013_p2:
    kai "I… I liked my quiet better. Hanging out with you around town was a nice distraction. For a while. Lately, though… it's just gotten exhausting."

translate en b29r_014:
    "Every word cuts straight through both of them. Yara takes a step back. Her face drains of color; tears catch the late afternoon light in her eyes."

translate en b29r_015:
    yara "{i}(whispering, voice cracking at the end){/i} A nice distraction…? {i}(letting out a bitter laugh, wiping her eyes with the back of her hand){/i} You really are the most selfish person I've ever met, Kai."

translate en b29r_016:
    "Yara turns and walks off into the drizzle. Kai stays frozen beneath the gate, letting the rain soak his numb face."

translate en b29r_017:
    kai_hati "My stupid logic tells me I just did the right thing. Cutting the thread early so the goodbye later won't hurt as much. {i}(a long pause){/i} Then why does my chest feel like it's slowly dying… inside the silence I built myself?"

translate en b29s_001:
    "Word that Yara got in spreads fast — that's just how school works. And Kai discovers an annoying truth about himself: he can smile and tell Yara congratulations to her face, yet he can't stand hearing the details."

translate en b29s_002:
    yara "{i}(carrying a folder stuffed with forms){/i} Kai, did you know boarding houses in Yogya need to be scouted way back—"

translate en b29s_003:
    kai "{i}(way too fast){/i} Oh, gotta get to class. Bu Sarah's looking for me. {i}(walking away){/i}"

translate en b29s_004:
    yara "{i}(staring at his back){/i} …Bu Sarah doesn't even teach today."

translate en b29s_005:
    "Next day: train schedules. The day after: enrollment paperwork. Every time a topic even hints at Yogya, Kai finds an exit door. And Yara — who normally records every sound — starts picking up on this pattern too: the sound of Kai's footsteps walking away."

translate en b29s_006:
    yara "{i}(sitting on the porch step, without her recorder this afternoon){/i} I've noticed, lho. Every time I say \"Yogya,\" you suddenly get busy. Out of nowhere. Like the school bell, except you're the one ringing."

translate en b29s_007:
    kai "{i}(silent; doesn't argue){/i} …"

translate en b29s_008:
    yara "I'm not mad. I just want to know. You're happy I got in, right?"

translate en b29s_009:
    kai "Happy. Temenan happy. {i}(a long pause){/i} It's just… every time you talk about the details, my head jumps straight to a train platform. And I'm not ready to picture that every single day. So I bolt. Sepurane, Yar."

translate en b29s_010:
    yara "{i}(looking at him, then giving a small nod){/i} Okay. Thanks for telling me — no more running off from this one, alright? {i}(standing up, holding out her hand){/i} Tomorrow we still work on the sound map. As for the Yogya stuff… we'll take it in installments. Little by little. Like how you listen to tapes. Sixty seconds at a time."

translate en b29s_011:
    kai_hati "Sixty seconds at a time. {i}(smiling faintly){/i} She really always knows how to shrink big things down to a size I can handle."

translate en b30r_001:
    "That night, Yara replays all their recordings. The wind on Bukit Banyak. The creak of the library door. The iron clatter of an old train. And tucked between them, there's always Kai's steady breathing nearby — or his faint laugh when they almost tripped over the tripod."

translate en b30r_002:
    yara "{i}(yanking her headphones off, tossing them onto the desk; whispering to the quiet room){/i} He's so stiff. Like part of him just… vanished. {i}(pause){/i} People don't turn that cold overnight. Unless something got taken from him. Or he took something."

translate en b30r_003:
    "After school, Yara waits near the parking lot as it empties out. Kai walks up head down, bag over his shoulder. Yara steps in front of him — portable recorder and pocket mic in her right hand."

translate en b30r_004:
    yara "Kai. {i}(keeping her voice steady even though it's shaking){/i} Today near the flea market there's an old blacksmith shop, still using hand hammers. The clang of iron is so rhythmic — like an ancient heartbeat. Come sound-hunting with me. Just this once."

translate en b30r_005:
    "Kai stops. He looks at the microphone, then up at Yara's face. Yara takes a step closer, holding the mic toward Kai's chest."

translate en b30r_006:
    yara "{i}(her voice breaking){/i} Listen. This thing can pick up even the quietest frequency out there. So why is it that when I look at you now… I can't hear anything coming from you anymore? You're like a blank tape that got wiped clean, Kai."

translate en b30r_007:
    kai_hati "A blank tape that got wiped clean. {i}(pause — the line hits dead center on the hole in his head){/i} She has no idea how right she is. Part of me really did get erased. Right on top of that shop counter. By my own hand."

translate en b30r_008:
    kai "{i}(clenching his fists in his pockets, walking right past her without looking back){/i} Sorry, Yara. Our recordings are done."

translate en b30r_009:
    "Yara stands frozen in the middle of the empty parking lot, only the hollow afternoon breeze for company. And Kai walks home with her words stuck in his head like a tape that won't stop looping: {i}a blank tape that got wiped clean.{/i}"

translate en b30r_010:
    kai_hati "A blank tape. Wiped clean. {i}(sitting still for a long time, then picking up the little recorder he borrowed from Yara and never gave back){/i} …If I'm really like a blank tape, should be easy enough to prove. What does empty even sound like?"

translate en b30r_011a:
    "He presses the microphone against his chest. Through the headphones: {i}thump… thump… thump…{/i} — uneven, way too fast, like someone who just finished running. Or someone terrified."

translate en b30r_012a:
    kai_hati "It's there. The beat's still there. Messy, sure, still there. {i}(pause){/i} So I'm not empty yet. What's missing isn't the pulse. Just… the song. —I'll save this recording. Maybe someday I'll have the guts to let her hear it."

translate en b30r_011b:
    "Tick. Tick. Tick. Sixty full seconds, nothing else. Kai replays it twice."

translate en b30r_012b:
    kai_hati "Time keeps moving, neat and indifferent. Maybe that's the difference between me and a clock. A clock's never scared of the next minute. {i}(pause){/i} I'll save this recording. As a reminder: even silence makes a sound."

translate en b30r_011c:
    "Kai stares at the recorder for a long time, then sets it gently back into the drawer, like he's afraid anyone might hear it."

translate en b30r_012c:
    kai_hati "No. Not tonight. If I hit record and it really comes out empty… I'm not ready to hear the proof."

translate en b30s_001:
    kai "{i}(stopping at the mouth of the alley, staring at the ground){/i} …Dry. Pak, the alley's dry. That's a first."

translate en b30s_002:
    ageng "{i}(from inside the shop){/i} Sepurane, kid. Looks like this alley's taking a break from the rain. {i}(smiling){/i} Come on in. Shop's quiet today. Real quiet, not the kind you make up in your head."

translate en b30s_003:
    kai "{i}(smiling slightly, stepping inside){/i} You always have a line ready, Pak."

translate en b30s_004:
    "There aren't any other customers that afternoon. Kai helps Pak Ageng reorganize the regular cassette shelves — slow, steady work that doesn't ask anything of his head."

translate en b30s_005:
    ageng "Type I on the left. Keep the handwritten labels separate from the factory prints. {i}(pausing, looking at Kai){/i} You seem lighter lately. Still stopping by every day, yet you don't look like someone chasing something anymore."

translate en b30s_006:
    kai "Still scared, Pak. About August. {i}(sliding a cassette box into place){/i} Difference is… the fear isn't driving anymore. It's sitting in the back seat. Gets loud sometimes. My hands are on the wheel, though."

translate en b30s_007:
    ageng "{i}(nodding slowly, satisfied){/i} That's the most grown-up thing I've ever heard come out of you, kid. {i}(standing up, grabbing two cups){/i} Tea. Yara said she's stopping by after this — wants to show you her list of sounds for her Malang map. You're waiting for her, right?"

translate en b30s_008:
    kai "I'm waiting, Pak. {i}(smiling){/i} Whatever time we've got left… I want to actually be here for it. Not peeking at it through a tape."

translate en b30s_009:
    "Outside, sunset light starts painting the dry alley. The shop is quiet — in the right way: not because it's been abandoned, simply because it's calmly waiting for its people to show up."
